OVERVIEW: Upload DICOM instances using STOW-RS

Stores one or more DICOM files to a DICOMweb server.

Examples:
  dicom-wado store https://server/dicom-web file1.dcm file2.dcm
  dicom-wado store https://server/dicom-web study/*.dcm --study 1.2.3.4.5
  dicom-wado store https://server/dicom-web --input files.txt --batch 10

USAGE: dicom-wado store <base-url> [<files> ...] [--study <study>] [--input <input>] [--batch <batch>] [--token <token>] [--continue-on-error] [--verbose]

ARGUMENTS:
  <base-url>              DICOMweb server base URL
  <files>                 DICOM files to upload (optional if --input is used)

OPTIONS:
  --study <study>         Study Instance UID for targeted storage
  --input <input>         File containing list of DICOM files to upload (one
                          per line)
  --batch <batch>         Number of files to upload per batch (default: 10)
                          (default: 10)
  --token <token>         OAuth2 bearer token for authentication
  --continue-on-error     Continue on errors instead of stopping
  --verbose               Show verbose output including progress
  --version               Show the version.
  -h, --help              Show help information.

